  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Emergency Health interventions in remote hard to reach and Drought impacted areas of Eritrea</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The main objective of this project is to provide quality and integrated health and nutrition assistance to vulnerable people affected by drought. This WHO project provides immunization services to women and children, antenatal and post-natal care to pregnant women, as well as critical items for Neonatal Intensive Care Unit (NICU). The project supports 208,151 people, including 43,844 women, 164,282 children, 25 men and 9,784 persons with disabilities.</narrative>
  </description>
